think After ALES30 (the multi-slot rack) sent, weighed the next rung. A rack-to-text slot sheet would serialize kilobytes of PCM per slot — a genuinely new, heavier serialization surface, riskier than a clean composition. The ALES29 road-on named "let the graft or paste join rather than butt" — a pure composition of two proven modules.
think Recognized paste_join IS ALES29's stereo two-sided insert-join applied to ALES25's held span: the clipboard holds its two channels at one shared length, so handing left[0..held]/right[0..held] to insert_join_stereo with the same at/lead/trail crosses both seams of both channels equal-power, atomic, with the proven scratch-clip build — adding only the Empty guard, no new arithmetic, seam law, or bound.
think Chosen crux-first: closes the last butt on the paste side (the gesture reached for most), lowest-risk, purely local, no seam, no gate. lotus/paste_join.rye — PasteJoinError = error{Empty} || timeline.EditError; one fn paste_join(cb, master, at, lead, trail).
obs First build failed the crux case: an overlap of 2 (den=1) hits only the crossfade's pure endpoints, no interior equal-power sample, so no seam sample landed strictly inside the ±30000 extremes. Fixed by widening the master to 16 samples, the span to 8, and lead/trail to 4 (den=3, a genuine interior crossover). GREEN after that single fix.
obs Witness tools/ales_paste_join_witness.rish GREEN; TAME style bans clean on the scan roster; no new zero-assert ratchet, no usize, no bare memcpy. stereo_insert_join and clipboard reused whole. Purely local — no socket, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device, no real meter, no real speaker; every custody gate untouched.
